      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The village was named after insurance magnate Clement Stone, who bought most of the land when it was still corn fields.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stone_Park%2C_Illinois",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The area that is now Stone Park was first settled in the late 19th century, long before it became a town.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://wiki-cafe.win/index.php/From_Settlements_to_City:_The_Evolution_of_Stone_Park,_Illinois",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Railroads reached the region in the 1880s, linking residents to Chicago and spurring early growth.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://wiki-cafe.win/index.php/From_Settlements_to_City:_The_Evolution_of_Stone_Park,_Illinois",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Industrial parks helped shape Stone Park’s economy, with light manufacturing thriving alongside service‑oriented shops and restaurants.",
